Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: nx669j: park the USB DisplayPort switch

The REDMAGIC 6 has a Nubia DisplayPort switch on the USB-C data lines
(stock: nubia,usb_switch_dp; enable on GPIO 14, active low; mode on
GPIO 116). Nothing drives GPIO 14 here, so it floats low and the switch
stays enabled. That takes D+/D- away from the PMIC charger detection:
every charger reads as SDP and the ADSP caps the input at 500 mA, even
on a 9 V / 3 A USB-PD contract.

Park it off the way the stock driver does at probe. The input limit
goes from 500 mA to 3 A within seconds (about 13 W from the same
charger that gave 4.5 W).

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-nubia-nx669j.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-nubia-nx669j.dts
@@ -869,6 +869,26 @@
 	/* TZ-owned (fingerprint / eSE SPI), as on the Qualcomm MTP */
 	gpio-reserved-ranges = <52 8>;
 
+	/*
+	 * Nubia's DisplayPort switch on the USB-C data lines (stock:
+	 * nubia,usb_switch_dp; enable is active low). Left floating low it
+	 * takes D+/D- from the charger detection: every charger reads as SDP
+	 * and the ADSP caps input at 500 mA. Stock parks it off at boot.
+	 */
+	usb-dp-switch-en-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "usb-dp-switch-en-n";
+	};
+
+	usb-dp-switch-mode-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <116 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-low;
+		line-name = "usb-dp-switch-mode";
+	};
+
 	/* Speaker amplifiers' I2S (stock: pri_mi2s_*_active) */
 	pri_mi2s_active: pri-mi2s-active-state {
 		sck-pins {
